  "modified": "2026-11-23T19:44:40Z",
  "details": "- CVE-2026-6460: add downstream hardening: plans and portals holding values\n  of a row type, also nested in other row types at any depth, block\n  shape-changing ALTERs of that type; WITH HOLD cursors refuse FETCH/MOVE\n  once a row type of their held rows was altered; stale PL/pgSQL row and\n  record variables, and row type values nested in PL/pgSQL arrays and\n  records, are rejected, also at RETURN; ALTER COLUMN TYPE locks the row\n  type and the types depending on it, and recording a dependency on a type\n  locks that type (partial mitigation, not upstream Part B)",
